<article class="env-proposition" id="74FEA6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/74FEA6">Proposition <span data-tag="74FEA6">6.4.5.4</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $n$-topos, and let $0 \leq m \leq n$. Then the full subcategory $\tau _{\leq m-1} \calX $ spanned by the $(m-1)$-truncated objects is an $m$-topos. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $m = n = \infty $, the result is obvious. Otherwise, it follows immediately from $(2)$ of Theorem <a href="/tag/9E9B8F" data-tag="9E9B8F">6.4.1.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>